From 75c08d8278895605f1971a4888663f79016edeea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wray-lee <wray-lee@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:01:11 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(channels): actually show live reasoning, and strip
 provider tool markup

The live-reasoning path added with the Slack outbound stream only worked
for channels served by `daemon.processInboundMessage`, and the delivered
text still leaked a model's own text tool protocol. Three gaps:

- Telegram is served by `channel_loop.processTelegramMessage`, which
  built its `TagFilter` in the default strip mode and never consulted
  `streamsReasoning`, so the draft never showed the thinking even with
  `draft_previews` on. The loop now selects the passthrough the same way
  the daemon does, via a `think_mode` on `StreamCtx`.

- `SessionManager.streamsReasoning` returned false for a session that did
  not exist yet. Slack appends the thread ts to the session key, so a
  channel turn routinely looks up a session created by that very turn and
  every Slack message was stripped. An unknown key now reports the
  configured default.

- `TagFilter` only knew `<tool_call>`. A model that falls back to its own
  text tool protocol (DeepSeek DSML: a `<|DSML| calls>` block wrapping
  `<|DSML| invoke ...>` and its parameter values) had those bytes
  delivered to the channel. The filter now drops marker regions in both
  think modes, and `providers.helpers` - which produces the delivered
  text - drops them too, so the final message is clean on every channel
  even when nothing was streamed.

Validation: `zig build test --summary all` (7581 passed, 14 skipped, 0
leaked) and `zig fmt --check` on the changed files, both in the Zig
0.16.0 container.
---
